ands and Puerto Rico on obtaining full compliance with CDL requirements. Following a five-year grace period,...","summarySource":"crs","title":"To amend title 49, United States Code, to grant the United States Virgin Islands and Puerto Rico eligibility to issue commercial driver's licenses, and for other purposes.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5656"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":4,"crossPartyCosponsors":3,"id":"hr5409-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-16","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-16","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 5409","policyArea":"Health","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Social Security Act to reserve 5 percent of health profession opportunity grant funds for U.S. territories, makes the Northern Mariana Islands eligible for such grants, and guarantees at least 2 grants to eligible entities located in territories.","summarySource":"ai","title":"Territory Health Revitalization Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5409"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":20,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr5209-119","introducedDate":"2025-09-08","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-09-08","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 5209","policyArea":"Foreign Trade and International Finance","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Modifies special rules for Haiti under the Caribbean Basin Economic Recovery Act by extending preferential duty treatment through 2037, strengthening labor compliance requirements, and requiring the U.S. Trade Representative to provide technical assistance to increase and diversify Haitian exports to the United States.","summarySource":"ai","title":"HOPE for Haitian Prosperity Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/5209"},{"bipartisan":true,"cosponsors":1,"crossPartyCosponsors":1,"id":"hr4292-119","introducedD