gin Islands. Specifically, the bill expands an existing program that authorizes nonimmigrant visa waivers for nationals of certain countries to enter Guam or the Northern Mariana Islands to also authorize...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Virgin Islands Visa Waiver Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/362"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr363-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 363","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Territorial Economic Recovery Act This bill excludes the income of certain controlled foreign corporations in U.S. territories from the calculation of global intangible low-taxed income (GILTI) for federal tax purposes. Under current law, a U.S. shareholder of a controlled foreign corporation is required to include in gross income the GILTI of the shareholder. The calculation of GILTI is based,...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Territorial Economic Recovery Act","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/363"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr364-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 364","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Territorial Tax Equity and Economic Growth Act of 2025 This bill lowers the residency requirements and modifies the income sourcing rules related to taxation of income from U.S. territories. Currently, bona fide residents of a U.S. territory may exclude income sourced to the territory in calculating U.S. federal income tax. A bona fide resident of a territory is a person that, in part, is present...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Territorial Tax Equity and Economic Growth Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/364"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr365-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 365","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Territorial Tax Equity Parity Act of 2025 This bill modifies the income sourcing rules related to taxation of income from U.S. territories. Under the bill, income is U.S.-sourced income or effectively connected to a U.S. trade or business only if attributable to an office or fixed place of business in the United States. (Currently, income is sourced to a U.S. territory and, thus, may be excluded...","summarySource":"crs","title":"Territorial Tax Parity Act of 2025","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/365"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr366-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 366","policyArea":"Taxation","ranked":true,"stage":"introduced","summary":"Amends the Internal Revenue Code to direct federal fuel tax revenues collected on fuel produced in the Virgin Islands and entered into the United States to be covered into the Virgin Islands treasury instead of the federal treasury.","summarySource":"ai","title":"To amend the Internal Revenue Code of 1986 to cover into the treasury of the Virgin Islands revenue from tax on fuel produced in the Virgin Islands and entered into the United States.","type":"hr","url":"https://www.congress.gov/bill/119th-congress/house-bill/366"},{"bipartisan":false,"cosponsors":0,"crossPartyCosponsors":0,"id":"hr367-119","introducedDate":"2025-01-13","latestAction":{"actionDate":"2025-01-13","text":"Referred to the House Committee on Ways and Means."},"number":"HR 367","policyArea":"Tax